 "method": "Scanned sketches (pdftoppm 300 dpi) traced by image processing (dark outline mask, fill, mirror-symmetrised or right-half mirrored), then read into sharp-corner half profiles rounded to 5 mm. Sketches are to scale: the printed top width, bottom width and depth agree within 1% (IL: 0.80/0.57/0.60/0.90/1.10 all within 1%; IP medium within 1%; U wide soffit 3.20 m gives the name depth within 1%).",
 "geometry_notes": [
  "Only overall top width (upper wing), bottom width (lower wing) and depth are printed; every thickness, splay and chamfer is SCALED from the sketches (estimate, ±10–20 mm).",
  "The brochure says moulds allow +5 cm top-flange thickness, +3/+6 cm web and mixed wing geometries; the modelled outlines are the drawn standard ones.",
  "TPP inverted-I: the lower wing is 1.20–1.80 m 'equal to the distance between beams'; the sketches are drawn at 1.80 m (scaled), which is implemented. Page p5 scan is rotated ~0.8°, corrected before tracing.",
  "IP-200 designation read from context (label illegible); IP-255-A traced only on its right half, modelled as IP-235-A + 200 mm web (convention).",
  "Max series web widths trace as 188–206 mm; 200 mm (IP-200/235) and 190 mm (A series) adopted.",
  "U narrow series (TA90E, TA180.18E, TA240.18E; lower wing 1.85 m) not implemented: inner surface drawn dotted and not traceable. U medium series (lower wing 2.60 m) has no sketch.",
  "No section properties are published; areas are analytic only."
